    "synthesis_verdict": "Q_R(q) = Σ_λ dim_q(V_λ)·mult_R(λ) defines the q-deformed icosahedral character matrix's row sums; for A_5 the H-sector Q_H(q) = 2·[5]_q has closed-form h-expansion 10 + 10h² + 2h⁴ (by algebraic identity [5]_q = h⁴+5h²+5). The structural h⁴ coefficient is +2 — DIFFERENT in sign AND magnitude from the Borromean H_3 reference h⁴ = −3/4. This complements T5: the H-sector carries its own h⁴ structure, but in a different group algebra than the Borromean trace coefficient — the ratio +2/(−3/4) = −8/3 has no clean structural meaning. The Clifford excess identity Σ_R Q_R − Σ_λ dim_q = dim_q(λ_self-conj) holds to machine precision for both A_4 (excess = dim_q((2,2))) and A_5 (excess = dim_q((3,1,1))) — this is the Wedderburn decomposition's q-deformed signature: self-conjugate partitions split into 2 conjugate A_n irreps under Res^{S_n}_{A_n}, and the excess weighting tracks this splitting at q ≠ 1. The q-deformed icosahedral matrix is a well-defined object at q_0; its H-sector's h⁴ structure is internally clean but NOT linked to the 3-strand h⁴ obstruction."
